# Issue #54: Edit Deck's Search Text ignores case (the connection DLL's card-search.h) and, as Konami's did, filters
# the list shown, so Reset brings every card back. From the map, on a new key account's 498-card trunk (it holds
# B. Skull Dragon, Dark Red Enchanter and Gaia the Dragon Champion).
click 60 752                     # Main Menu
sleep 1.5
click 120 338                    # Edit Deck
expect component DeckEditTest 20
sleep 3
click 1000 88                    # Reset: every card in the trunk (nothing to undo on a fresh editor)
sleep 2

# Lowercase finds the capitalised names.
click 960 57                     # Search Text
sleep 1.5
click 700 98                     # the text box (it keeps the last search: clear it)
key End BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace
type dragon
click 578 205                    # Card Search
expect flash "B. Skull Dragon"
expect flash "Gaia the Dragon Champion"
shot card-search-dragon

# A second search looks only inside the first one's results: "red" keeps B. Skull Dragon (its text names Red-Eyes),
# not Dark Red Enchanter, which isn't a Dragon card.
click 960 57
sleep 1.5
click 700 98
key End BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace
type red
click 578 205
expect flash "B. Skull Dragon"
expect no-flash "Dark Red Enchanter"

# Reset, then the same search finds both.
click 1000 88                    # Reset: the whole trunk again, Tainted Wisdom first
expect flash "Tainted Wisdom"
click 960 57
sleep 1.5
click 700 98
key End BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace BackSpace
type red
click 578 205
expect flash "Dark Red Enchanter"
shot card-search-red
